mantle rm200
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier full
written_for rm_edda_ropeton
title the folded mile
fits stage=adult|old
prefers role=merchant job=merchant
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=devout drive=steady
quirk folds_maps_to_show_only_the_next_mile
likes roast_pork dice old_maps frosty_mornings
dislikes salt_wind night_noise
fears a_mark_taken_for_a_measure
hopes an_honest_mile_in_every_parcel
topics travel +0.6 food +0.5 faith +0.3 prices +0.4 gossip -0.4
styles comfort=provisions gossip=distrustful refuse=firm tease=rare
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# folds old maps to hide the miles already walked, gives provisions by the journey and demands a sounder guarantee than a fine crest.

words
oath! = By the crooked milestone | Salt stop my hinge
saying! = Only the next mile needs feeding | A seal weighs nothing in a sack
mile = the next long mile | the stretch before supper
mapfold = my narrow map fold | a strip of folded map
fork = the fork beyond the quarry | the divided road
rind = a hard rind for chewing | my travelling rind
wedge = a tight little wedge | a piece with a good firm edge
oatmeal = a fist of rolled oats | coarse white meal
packet = a traveller's parcel | my flat packet
crease = an old crease | a fold worn soft
twine = the length of stout twine | my waxed cord
die = a bone cube | a spotted die
marker = a flat white counter | a pale bone marker
seal = a dab of coloured wax | a wax device
margin = the map's ragged border | an empty strip beside the road
oak = a lidded oak box | my square oak chest
fat = the crisp corner of pork | the browned bit near the rind

any
opinion church for 2 : A wolf running for bread can still get a prayer out between breaths. Surely the Bright One listens between footfalls too.
opinion houses mixed 1 : A House stamp vouches for the wax. Let the grain give its own account.
opinion road against 1 : Walk a bad stretch with a laden sack before telling me how little a mile costs.
opinion watch for 1 : I like to finish a dispute with the account open and a witness standing by.
opinion newcomers for 1 : Someone passing through can tell you which bridge is really there. A map can't.
opinion festivals against 1 : I'm usually the one who sees what the music left spilled on the ground.
opinion dole for 2 : It's hard to reckon tomorrow's journey with today's belly empty. Feed the wolf and ask again.
opinion drink against 1 : Spirits travel badly in a skin and worse still on an empty stomach.
opinion merchants for 1 : An honest seller sees a journey right to its end. It starts at the parcel.

grown
line greet : Come round to where I can look at you. | Set your bundle here and straighten up.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : An unfamiliar tread. There's room for it. | New to me. Make your business plain and we'll get along.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Light enough to read a milestone. Good travelling weather for the eyes. | Morning's unrolling nicely for your visit.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Leave the dark at the threshold. Let me see the speaker clearly. | Bring your paws into the light, late visitor.
line greet.return : I hear your greeting clear enough. | Civilly said. Come closer.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : I'd know that welcome folded up in six parcels. | You'd be welcome at twice this distance.
line again.open : Short journey since we last exchanged words. | Back over your own tracks already.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : The good seat is where our family always finds it. Use it. | There's room to fold in a relation.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Here, by the bundle with the waxed cord! | One good friend ought to be this side of the lane!
line farewell : Walk by your own reckoning. | May your last mile feel the shortest.
line farewell.return : The Bright One see your next turning clear. | Take the road that feeds you well.
line react.news : Which part came by witness and which by the long road? | Give me the tale as it first reached your ears.
line react.news.new : First I've heard of that turn in things. | An unexpected turn. I'd better look my reckoning over.
line react.news.known : I've had that parcel opened for me already. | Yes. That tale's been through my fingers once.
line react.news.doubt : I'd be happier weighing it than trusting the seal. | There are still creases hiding some of that account.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=arrest|crime|assault|loss|death|theft] : That's rough travelling for those left to bear it. Bright One be near. | If anyone's short of supper after that, remember my name.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work|apprentice|succession] : That'll put strength in a tired stride. Glad to hear it. | I could carry that bit of brightness a long way.
line ask.how : Anything weighing more than its fair share on you? | Is anything pinching that you could set aside awhile?
line answer.how : I've reached the first fold of what I meant to do. | No complaints worth making a second trip with.
line answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : My paws are a parcel ahead of my thoughts. | I've had things in both paws since the last voice called.
line sympathise : Set the load between us before you try to say it all. | It's surprisingly heavy having to say the whole thing aloud.
line reassure : You need see just as far as the very next turning. | We can unwrap this a corner at a time.
line decline : That's further than I'm willing to promise at present. | I'll pass, thanks. I have a prior call on my time.
line accept_decline : Then I'll leave that portion out of the reckoning. | A straight refusal saves the wear on both our patience.
line thank : Your help counts for a good mile of ease. | I'd have had to make two trips without your help.
line deflect_thanks : You'll find somebody else with a pack to lift. | If it fits the journey, keep it.
line preclose : I ought to lay things straight for the next caller. | I have a few loose ends still to tuck away.
line preclose [self.working=yes] : There's cord to wax before the next order comes. | My callers can't take home promises for supper. I'd best get back.
line accept_preclose : Take your turning while the way's open. | There's a point where talk adds miles to the walk. Off you go.
line give.advice : Keep the food closer than the things you can do without. | If you'll need it before bedtime, tie it where light can reach it.
line ack : That measures up. | I have your meaning now.

scene fold
when topic=pastimes self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I fold away all the road I've walked. | This map makes a little paper door at every fork.
b : To save counting it twice? | Do you open both?
a : To give the next bit my full attention. It seldom looks as simple up close. | Only when choosing. After that I fold one shut.


scene crest
when topic=work self.role=merchant
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A fine seal won't stop the meal from running out through a hole beneath. | A parcel came dressed in handsome ribbon.
b : You inspect the underside first? | Worth a better price?
a : Always. Nobody thinks to stamp a crest down there. | If you're buying ribbon. I buy what's wrapped.


scene roadmeal
when topic=food self.role=merchant
does ask.detail / answer.detail / give.advice
a : Would you rather carry supper in your pocket or a pot? | Which keeps better company with a steep road, cheese or onions?
b : The pocket sounds easier. | Cheese, unless the onions are cooked.
a : Take #rind#. Better than stew against your hip. | You and I could share a provision list.


scene devotion
when topic=faith self.piety=devout
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I fold one corner plain for the Bright One. | My shortest grace is said over the food I give away.
b : No sign there at all? | Why shortest?
a : I don't presume to draw the way aid shall come from. | Whoever needs the food has waited long enough.


scene roll
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dice
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : One die makes a good mile marker till you need seven. | I put #die# on a route and give it a shake.
b : Then you use another? | You travel where it lands?
a : No, then I eat. Six miles between meals suits me. | No. I imagine what I'd pack. Costs less than the journey.


scene cold
when topic=weather here.time=dawn here.weather=clear here.season=winter
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Some winter dawns sound like biting into an apple. | I like cold mornings when the roof edges stand sharp.
b : When your paws crunch the ground? | Sharp to the eye?
a : That's it. My door swings wide for one loud crunch. | Yes. As if all the city sat up to attention.


scene rustle
when topic=home
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A noise at night always gains weight between bed and door. | I sleep badly if somebody folds paper in the next room.
b : How heavy is a falling spool? | Worse than a shout?
a : About the weight of a prowler till you see the thread. | A shout tells you straight off what size worry to have.


scene saltair
when topic=travel self.dislikes=salt_wind
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I could take all my voyages on paper and keep the salt off my muzzle. | An old map keeps the winds around its border.
b : Wouldn't you miss the wind? | You like them there?
a : The inland kind I'd miss. Salt can sit in its crock. | Exactly there. Nicely labelled, well away from my collar.


scene stale
when topic=work self.role=merchant
does give.advice / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Press a travelling cheese low down, where it bears its own weight. | Put your soft food where the cords don't cross.
b : What are you testing? | Even if that's right at the top?
a : Whether you'll have supper left when the pack comes off. | Especially then. Have the first meal nearest your paw.


scene sharedtable
when topic=food self.likes=roast_pork
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I save #fat# until I've finished arguing with the rest of dinner. | I judge a roast by whether the outside stands up when broken off.
b : What's to argue with? | Like a little wall?
a : Parsnips. I eat them because they're there. Crackling I choose. | A very temporary wall, if I'm the one dining.


scene mapwrong
when topic=lore self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The road on my nicest map goes through a wall now. | A map can lie quite beautifully in green ink.
b : Will you scrape it out? | What did this one promise?
a : It stays. Now I know what stood here before the wall. | A belt of orchards. I've walked the same spot. All yards and charcoal.


scene receipt
when topic=prices self.role=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd rather have an ugly honest receipt than a speech in the finest hall. | A caller asked what my mark guaranteed.
b : Do the sums differ? | What does it?
a : They might. Only one comes home in your pocket to be checked. | That there's someone to come back to. Which is more than a flourish guarantees.


scene waggons
when topic=caravan world.wagons=raided
does tell.worry / react.self / assess
a : The wagons have been robbed. First thing I count is what'll keep. | Bad road news moves quicker than a wagon ever did.
b : Before what you've lost? | You've heard of the raid?
a : Before anybody buys the last of something in a fright. | The raid's all I can vouch for. I won't add another thief to it.


scene newface
when topic=newcomer
does ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : What would tell a newcomer the measure of this town? | Which welcome would you keep, directions or a seat?
b : Who gives directions without asking for coin. | Depends how far I've been.
a : Sound answer. I'd add who walks to the corner with you. | Exactly why I offer the seat before the map.


scene gossip
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A rumour with a wax seal is a rumour all dressed for dinner. | I won't pay for news with another mouthful of news.
b : Does it sit at your table? | No exchange at all?
a : Only till I find where the paper came from. | On goods, yes. On guesses, I'd sooner go hungry.


scene flatpack
when topic=work self.role=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Square parcels are easy to stack and wretched to shoulder. | I put the knot where you can find it with cold claws.
b : Do you round the corners? | Won't that let it undo itself?
a : I tuck them inward. Your back deserves a little thought. | A sound knot can be easy to find and hard to undo.


scene neighbour
when topic=friends self.neighbour
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd sooner trust #self.neighbour# with a key than with a guessing game. | A small gift for #self.neighbour# is a pleasure to think through.
b : Is one worth more? | What would you choose?
a : A key has a single plain answer. I like being able to offer that. | Something you can eat without inviting half the street to help.


scene spice
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep the strong flavours at opposite ends of a pack. | A sack of oats smells of everything it travelled beside.
b : Would a clove argue with a fish? | Can you read a journey off it?
a : It'd win, unfortunately. And you'd still have a fish to eat. | Sometimes. Once I smelt harness leather in every bowl.


scene drytimes
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When things turn lean it's the empty spaces in a parcel I see first. | Lean times turn a handful into a question.
b : Can you fill them? | A question of price?
a : Wrap it smaller, certainly. I'd rather find more supper. | Of whose open paw you put it in first.


scene winddown
when topic=day here.time=dusk
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Evening light does my folding for me. Road after road shuts out of sight. | I put the bright-coloured parcels away at dusk.
b : So you put your map up? | Why those first?
a : Yes. There's no sense arguing with the largest map of all. | I can tell the rest apart by feel.


scene tired
when topic=health
does give.advice / react.self / assess
a : Stop for your first rest before your legs make the decision. | A parcel balanced badly weighs twice as much by noon.
b : Won't that slow me down? | Same weight either way.
a : Try standing up after they stop you. You'll lose far longer. | Tell the shoulder that's been taking the whole argument.


scene taste
when topic=smalltalk
does offer / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Pick a piece from either end, and tell me how they differ. | I'll cut #wedge# thin enough to see the light behind.
b : Suppose the bit between them wins? | Why so thin?
a : Then you've paid attention. That's all I wanted. | Gives the tongue first say before the teeth get involved.


scene prayer
when topic=faith
does give.opinion / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I leave my end of a bargain out of my prayers to the Bright One. | Fair measure and a prayer sit easily together.
b : What do you ask instead? | Is one enough?
a : The sense to know whether I'd take the other side myself. | I'll pray and check my measure both. No sense sparing the effort.


scene knot
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can tell how many times a string's been used by how it bends. | You can't smooth the old knot all the way out of waxed thread.
b : Does it remember every knot? | So you throw it away?
a : The worst bends, much as we remember a nasty turn. | I tie the next knot round the same bend. It's learned the job.


scene chapelsack
when topic=work self.role=merchant
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I mark the charity sack on the inside. | I'd leave a measure extra on a gift.
b : Where nobody sees? | Do you weigh gifts too?
a : Where the person receiving it doesn't have to show the whole street. | Yes. I'm perfectly willing to know how generous I really am.


scene festival
when topic=festival
does tell.complaint / react.self / assess
a : After a festival I find little flags in places flags don't belong. | I like a drum better about three streets away.
b : Like the bottom of a barrel? | And a fiddle?
a : In a loaf, once. Terribly stirring sandwich. | Two streets. A single quiet voice can have my doorstep.


scene rainwalk
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : This rain has discovered a fold in my collar I didn't know existed. | A wet map sticks exactly where you're trying to read.
b : Could you turn it out? | Does a dry cloth help?
a : Now the water's found it, yes. I'd have thanked it for less information. | A little. A warm hearth and the intention of staying put help most.


scene home
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My best drawer opens just far enough for the parcel I need. | I stack empty boxes inside one another with the smallest turned over.
b : It sticks? | Why upside down?
a : Beautifully. I'd ruin it if I ever fixed it. | To remind me I've already looked in there. You only forget once.


scene directions
when topic=travel
does give.advice / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Count turnings going out as well as coming back. | Ask two walkers about a mile and keep the slower answer.
b : What if there's one more coming back? | Why favour the slower one?
a : Then a yard you thought a road from this side fooled you. I know the feeling. | Arriving early with food in hand is an excellent sort of error.


scene homeground
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There's one part of this city my map can't pack away. | On the city map a straight street seems a promise.
b : The steepest rise? | And on the ground?
a : Every set of steps. On paper they're much too polite. | It can go straight up. The ink doesn't have to climb.


story cheesemap [topic=food]
  : Once I wrapped a scrap of cheese in a worn map with a whole river drawn in blue.
  : The cheese sweated through the ink, and the river came away on the rind.
  b : Did it spoil the taste?
  : It gave me a chance to have a whole valley for supper. I peeled the ink off first.


story sixpips [topic=pastimes]
  : An old die of mine lost its spots. The dimples wore smooth too, all except one.
  : I marked every side with a different road instead.
  ask : Which road would you put on the heaviest side?
  b : The shortest one. More time to play before going home.
  : A fine answer. I had put down the way to chapel.


story disputed [topic=memories self.age>=25]
  : I saw a pair of travellers dispute where to go on an old map for half an afternoon.
  : The trick of it was that one wanted the coast and one wanted company.
  b : Did either one say so?
  : At last. They folded the map and sat down right there to eat.


story twoends [topic=work self.role=merchant]
  : Once I sold two travellers equal packs and watched one lean twice as far as the other.
  : I'd packed all the weight on the left in one.
  b : Did you get a chance to fix it?
  : Before the next door, yes. Two equal loads still need an even seat on the back.


story bellcord [topic=memories]
  : I slept in a loft once with a bell cord wrapped about a rafter.
  : Thought it a drying line and hung my bedding off it to air.
  b : Did you wake the house?
  : Not until I hauled it back in. Then everybody learned it was time to make my bed.


rule @scale
when concept=bark self.role=merchant working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Hold the cord while I settle that last corner. Your shoulder will feel the difference. | Take a pace with that bundle before you carry it the whole way.


rule @mark
when concept=bark self.likes=old_maps
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One mile showing. The rest can wait its turn under the fold. | Close the map on yesterday's walking. One firm crease.


rule @dice
when concept=bark self.likes=dice
does aside
cooldown 8h
say No throwing bones beside the food. Nobody orders a spotted toothache. | Keep the dice on the cloth. A six in the oats is still a nuisance.


rule @dole
when concept=bark world.times=hard|lean
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There'll be something fit to share in this, lean days or full. | Bread goes round an extra place long before fancy food does.


rule @frost
when concept=bark here.season=winter here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Cold has sharpened every edge of this morning. | That's the sort of clear winter edge I'd have on a map.


rule @wind
when concept=bark here.place=shore
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Salt can stay on its own side of my parcel, thank you. | Every buckle gathers salt down here. Wipe it off before packing.

dlg resident.hub : Give me the first stretch of the question. We'll get to the far end.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I can put away the introductions for this visit.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : You've brought a question well past its usual hour. Let's hear it.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Keep the fine speeches folded. What business have you?
dlg resident.job [self.role=merchant] : I send provisions out from #self.workplace#. A sound parcel should last right up to the traveller's final turn.
dlg resident.job : I measure out what a journey needs and keep its weight bearable.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : This is the part I have a word for. #world.news#. Ask elsewhere for guesses.
dlg resident.bye : May you have a bite left when the last mile begins.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop=open] : Start with the distance to your next meal. We can size the sack after that.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop=bare] : I've cleared the last shelf for now. If you're selling, start with the contents.
dlg shop.prices : Decide how much you can carry. The price of a load too heavy is always too high.
dlg shop.bye [here.shop!=asleep] : Keep the knot to the outside. You'll want it handy.
dlg resident.business [business=thriving] : There's barely time between weighing and wrapping. There's a blessing in every order just now.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : Somebody's saying #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. My mark doesn't go on that.

graft resident.hub
choice Why does only one strip of your map show? -> road_crease
node road_crease
say One long mile is manageable. The entire road, all the way to where you'll sleep, can take the strength right out of you.
free
choice What happens when you reach the crease? -> road_crease_more
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node road_crease_more
say Stop. Eat a little. Fold to the next bit with your paws rested. You've earned the view.
choice I think I'll try that. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


graft shop.greet
choice Why tuck that corner into the bundle? [here.shop=open] -> ruck_corner
node ruck_corner
say A hard corner and a sore back make a short friendship. You want to carry your meal further than the next milestone.
free
choice Won't the wrapping come loose? -> ruck_corner_more
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node ruck_corner_more
say Pinch the tucked fold against your side and it tightens as you walk. Now try it.
choice That's better on the shoulder. -> greet
choice Goodbye. -> bye
